\f1\fs22 The Domain concert's unexpected fusion of Airborne and Cloudborne proved merely the opening act of what Gerry Hardman later termed "a societal annoyance cascade." By morning, thousands of young people from both sides of the Layer converged on Bent Street, the corporate corridor housing Tramp Tower\'97the gleaming eighty-story spire of Ulyssia's corporate police headquarters.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>What began as a disorganized mass of disaffected youth rapidly evolved into something more structured. Makeshift tents appeared, constructed from expensive Airborne designer fabrics and repurposed Cloudborne industrial tarps. Communal kitchens served both imported Airborne delicacies and Cloudborne street food. Improbable friendships formed between Airborne trust fund activists and Cloudborne service workers, united by their newfound sense of generational solidarity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Signs ranged from the profound ("The Layer Is In Our Minds") to the profane ("Tax The Rich Or Eat Them"). The most popular placards featured rhinestone-decorated outlines of the Gyges Disc with slogans like "Transparency For The 1%" and "Your Stasis Technology Is Our Shared Future."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A stage cobbled together from shipping pallets and exhibition booth components became the protest's focal point. Throughout the day, speakers alternated with musicians, most mimicking the Evolution Elvi's style, but with increasingly political overtones.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Inside Tramp Tower, corporate police executives stared down from their climate-controlled offices, bewildered by the swelling crowd. Mid-level managers frantically compiled reports assessing "demographic cohesion threats" and "cross-class contamination indices."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry Hardman observed it all from his sixty-eighth floor corner office, occasionally glancing at the operation plans for the TMinus-Virus deployment sitting on his desk. He'd canceled three meetings already, unwilling to leave his window as the situation evolved below.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sir," his assistant interrupted via intercom, "the CEO is demanding an update on the 'hippie situation,' his words."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Tell him it's being monitored," Gerry replied, watching as a new band took the makeshift stage below.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The group\'97five Airborne university students and three Cloudborne service workers who had apparently met just twelve hours earlier\'97called themselves "The Revolutionary Blue Suede." Their instruments were an odd mix of expensive Airborne electronic equipment and modified Cloudborne household items converted into percussion instruments.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As they launched into their set, the crowd began to coalesce, moving rhythmically as the familiar melody of the Elvi hit began. But the lyrics that emerged sparked confusion in Tramp Tower's upper floors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What are they saying?" demanded Deputy Director Plaskow, squinting through the polarized glass.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Something about 'piglicious minds,'" replied his analyst, adjusting the directional microphone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Indeed, the crowd below had erupted into a unified chorus of what was clearly a reworked version of the Evolution Elvi's hit. The chorus thundered up the sides of Tramp Tower:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We can't go on together With piglicious minds! And we can't build our future With piglicious minds!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Verses about police brutality, corporate surveillance, and economic inequality replaced the original anti-religious themes, but maintained the same infectious melody and rhythm. The crowd chanted the refrain with increasing volume, their voices bouncing off the glass facades of corporate headquarters lining Bent Street.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Inside Tramp Tower, confusion reigned. Emergency meetings were called to decipher the meaning of "piglicious." Security analysts frantically searched databases for known protest terminologies. Legal teams prepared injunctions against undefined offenses.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What the tax is a piglicious mind?" demanded CEO Dunhilton when Gerry finally answered his call. "Is this some kind of Cloudborne slang we should be concerned about? Is it a reference to law enforcement?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I believe, sir," Gerry replied with his characteristic measured tone, "it's a portmanteau of 'pig'\'97a derogatory term for police\'97and 'malicious' or possibly 'suspicious.' It's meant to criticize corporate police thinking."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Well, it's ridiculous," Dunhilton sputtered. "Linguistic abominations! In my day, protesters at least had the decency to use proper grammar when undermining authority."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Outside, the protest continued to grow. As it did, the groundswell changes the name of the movement from Occupy Bent Street to \'93Get Bent Street\'94.News feeds across Ulyssia showed split-screen images: the unruly yet peaceful crowd on one side, Pastor Humble's latest revival meeting on the other. The society's fracturing was being broadcast in real-time, different kinds of fervor taking hold at opposite ends of the ideological spectrum.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>By nightfall, the protest had developed its own rituals. Every hour, on the hour, the crowd would fall silent, raise their hands, and wiggle their fingers in what they called "consensus approval"\'97an ancient protest gesture unearthed from historic records. Corporate police officers positioned around the perimeter watched with increasing unease as Airborne youth taught Cloudborne workers hand signals for various protest maneuvers.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry Hardman remained at his window long after most executives had gone home, watching as the protesters set up projection equipment and began displaying images of the High Elvis's concert on the side of an adjacent building. Below him, thousands of voices once again joined in the chorus of "Piglicious Minds," the word now emblazoned on hastily printed t-shirts and spray-painted on the barricades.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He picked up the TMinus-Virus deployment plans, considering the complications this new development created. The targeted virus had been designed specifically for Elvi genetic markers, but with Airborne and Cloudborne youth now intermixed with the Evolution Elvi, collateral impact would be unavoidable.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the protest below settled in for the night, constructing sleeping areas segregated by nothing but preference rather than class, Gerry made a note in the operation file: "Social mutation observed. Recommendation: viral deployment recalibration."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Outside, the last performance of the night concluded with the crowd chanting in unified voice: "We stand against oppression! Praise the Holy Momma! Praise the Dawkins. Praise the revolution!"\

